## 4. Envelope + conventions (confirmed)

Confirmed from `/v1/api/payment-link/` spec:

```ts
type ApiEnvelope<T> = {
  success: true;
  timestamp: string;   // ISO 8601
  message?: string;
  data: T;
};
// Error shape on non-2xx — TBD, will confirm on first 4xx response.
```

**Conventions:**
- **URL prefix:** All endpoints live under `/v1/api/...` — `API_BASE_URL` does **not** include `/v1`, so domain modules write paths like `/v1/api/payment-link/`. Trailing slashes appear in spec — preserve them.
- **Money:** Integer cents. Field names use `_cents` suffix (`amount_cents`, `min_amount`, `max_amount`). Convert at the boundary — the rest of the app stays in dollars.
- **Dates:** ISO 8601 strings. The rest of the app uses unix-ms `number` — convert at the boundary.
- **Casing:** Easy API uses `snake_case` everywhere. Map to `camelCase` in domain modules.

When wiring the typed wrapper to [lib/easy-api/server.ts](lib/easy-api/server.ts), have it unwrap `.data` on success so domain code returns plain `T` (still inside the `EasyApiResponse` discriminated union).

